melody:
# Refrain (the original is in cut time; written here with quarter-note beats)
Though A-pril
D4 C#4 D4
show-ers may come your way,
A4(2) A4(2) ~A4 D4 C#4 D4 B4(4) ~B4
they bring the flow-ers that bloom in May.
D4 C#4 D4 C5(2) C5(2) ~C5 D4 C#4 D4 D5(4) ~D5
So if it's rain-ing, have no re-grets,
B4 C5 D5 D5(2) E4(2) ~E4 D5 C5 B4 C5(4) ~C5
be-cause it is-n't rain-ing rain, you know,
E4 F#4 G4 B4 E5 E5 B4 B4 E5 E5
(it's rain-ing vi-o-lets,)
B4 B4 A#4 A4 G4 A4/ r/
and where you see clouds up-on the hills,
D4 C#4 D4 A4(2) A4(2) ~A4 D4 C#4 D4 B4(4) ~B4
you soon will see crowds of daf-fo-dils,
E4 D#4 E4 B4(2) B4(2) ~B4 E4 D#4 E4 C5(4) ~C5
so keep on look-ing for a blue-bird,
E4 D#4 E4 C5 A4 B4 A4 D5 C5(2)
and list'-ning for his song,
A4 B4 D5 G4 A4 B4(3)
when-ev-er A-pril show-ers come a-long.
G4 E4 F#4 E4 F#4 E4 D4 A4 B4 G4(4) ~G4(2) r(2)
